      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-17-trellis-ai-yc-w24-hiring-a-product-lead-to-build-agents-for-",
      "title": "Trellis AI (YC W24)  hiring a product lead to build agents for healthcare access",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/trellis-ai/jobs/Cg94htp-product-lead\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48573221\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Trellis builds and deploys AI agents that help patients access life-saving therapies.\nOur platform automates the complex administrative workflows that stand between patients and treatment, including document intake, prior authorizations, appeals, reimbursement research, and coverage determination. Today, our self-improving AI agents process billions of dollars in therapies annually and support patients across all 50 states.\nFounded out of the Stanford AI Lab, Trellis combines cutting-edge AI with deep healthcare expertise to solve one of the largest operational challenges in healthcare: getting patients the care they need, faster. We work with leading healthcare organizations to streamline operations, reduce administrative burden, and accelerate access to treatment at scale.\nWe’re backed by leading investors including General Catalyst, YC, Telesoft Partners, and executives from Google and Salesforce. Over the past year, we’ve experienced exceptional growth, scaling revenue rapidly while expanding our footprint across specialty healthcare markets.\nJoining Trellis means working at the intersection of AI, healthcare, and company-building. You’ll partner directly with the founders, help shape the next phase of growth, and see the real-world impact of your work in the number of patients who receive critical treatment because of the systems we build.\nOwn Product Strategy and Execution\nAs Product Lead, you'll drive product development from concept through launch and iteration. You'll work directly with customers, engineers, and leadership to identify opportunities, validate solutions, and bring new products to market.\nYou'll own major product initiatives end-to-end, leading 0→1 product development while ensuring existing products continue to evolve alongside customer needs and advances in AI capabilities.\nYou'll work closely with the CEO and leadership team to shape company strategy, product direction, and go-to-market priorities.\nWork Directly With Customers and C-Suite\nYou will spend significant time with customers across healthcare organizations, including executives, operations teams, and technical stakeholders.\nUnderstand customer workflows, requirements, and operational challenges\nIdentify bottlenecks and opportunities for automation\nRun discovery sessions and gather product feedback\nDesign and present product demos\nPartner with customers during implementation and rollout\nAct as a trusted advisor on AI adoption and workflow transformation\nBuild deep relationships that influence both product direction and company strategy\n5+ years building and shipping technical products\nPrevious experience as a Product Manager, Product Lead, Founder, FDE or equivalent role\nStrong product intuition with a track record of turning ambiguous problems into successful products\nExcellent communication skills across technical and non-technical audiences\nAbility to influence executive stakeholders and build alignment across teams\nExperience working directly with customers and translating customer needs into product strategy\nComfort operating in fast-moving, highly ambiguous startup environments\nStrong understanding of AI technologies and their practical applications\nBachelor's degree in a technical, business, or related field (or equivalent practical experience)\nExperience building AI agents, workflow automation systems, or LLM-powered products\nHealthcare, health-tech, or other complex regulated-industries experience\nAbility to prototype products using modern AI coding tools\nExperience writing or reviewing code, particularly Python or Typescript\nConsulting, solutions engineering, or other customer-facing experience\nStartup experience in high growth early-stage environments",
