      "id": "theverge-2026-06-17-the-best-early-amazon-prime-day-deals-so-far",
      "title": "The best early Amazon Prime Day deals so far",
      "summary": "The products pictured here aren’t on sale, but we certainly hope they will be soon. | Image: Alex Parkin / The Verge\t\n\nAmazon’s earlier-than-usual Prime Day doesn’t begin until June 23rd, but there are several even earlier deals on must-have products that you can check out right now. To name some examples, Apple’s AirPods Pro 3 are selling at their cheapest-ever price. Also, you can grab Ring’s la",
      "body": "Amazon’s earlier-than-usual Prime Day doesn’t begin until June 23rd, but there are several even earlier deals on must-have products that you can check out right now. To name some examples, Apple’s AirPods Pro 3 are selling at their cheapest-ever price. Also, you can grab Ring’s latest battery-powered doorbell for $60 off and it includes a free Indoor Cam Plus with purchase.\nWhile the pre-Prime Day deals are looking good so far, you may not see the brands or products you’re looking for — hopefully, those deals will come later in June. Still, we’ve only included early deals that meet the criteria we hold for all our commerce coverage: they’re good products sold at attractive prices.\nWe’ll update this post frequently ahead of Prime Day.\nRing Battery Doorbell Plus (second-gen)\nBose QuietComfort Ultra headphones (second-gen)\n[Product: Lego Ideas - Van Gogh “Starry Night” set | https://www.amazon.com/LEGO-6386348-TBD-Ideas-21333/dp/B09SM828FD?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=nOD/rLJHOac&mid=13923&murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-us%2Fproduct%2Fvincent-van-gogh-the-starry-night-21333]\n* For a limited time, you can get a $15 promotional gift card when you buy a $100 Newegg gift card. It’s always nice to get a little more for your money, especially if you plan to buy pricey PC components, be it RAM, an SSD, or a graphics card.\n* Fitbit’s Charge 6 fitness tracker has dropped to its lowest price yet at Amazon, costing $79.99 (originally $159.99, but usually around $100). It’s a solid alternative to Google’s $99 and screenless Fitbit Air. The 2023 Charge 6 features an OLED screen, a haptics-based button, plus the ability to ping you with notifications. Read our review.\n[Product: Logitech MX Master 3S | https://www.amazon.com/Logitech-Wireless-Ultra-fast-Scrolling-Bluetooth/dp/B09HM94VDS?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Flogitech-mx-master-3s-wireless-usb-a-laser-mouse-with-ultrafast-scrolling-wireless-black%2FJ7H7ZY8XTK, https://logitech.cfzu.net/c/482924/499820/8585?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.logitech.com%2Fen-us%2Fshop%2Fp%2Fmx-master-3s-mac-bluetooth-mouse.910-006569]\n* The Baseus AM52 10,000mAh power bank that can deliver Qi2.2 25W wireless charging speeds is cheaper than ever for Verge readers. Through June 30th, you can head over to Amazon and use the code THEVERGECODE to nab one for $42.99 — considerably cheaper than the $63.99 price that Prime members have access to. Read about the AM52’s performance here.\n[Product: Eero Pro 6E tri-band router | https://www.amazon.com/eero-reliable-gigabit-connect-Coverage/dp/B091G65HH6?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Feero-pro-6e-tri-band-mesh-wi-fi-6e-system-3-pack-white%2FJ39QV82L2X, https://www.amazon.com/eero-reliable-gigabit-connect-Coverage/dp/B091G64GVK/?tag=theverge02-20]\n* Amazon’s Fire 7 Kids tablet is steeply discounted ahead of Prime Day. The 32GB tablet that includes a bumper case, one year of access to a suite of kid-friendly content, and a two-year hardware warranty is down to $64.99 at Amazon (originally $129.99). There’s nothing spectacular about the specs, but it’s a good-enough tablet to withstand whatever your kiddo does to it. The two-year warranty is “worry-free,” which Amazon defines as “if it breaks, we will replace it.” The 16GB version is $54.99.\n* Amazon’s Fire TV Soundbar Plus that also includes a wireless subwoofer and two satellite speakers is down to $379.99 (originally $489.99), it’s best price to date. It’s a solid sound system if you don’t want to spend a bunch of money. The soundbar supports HDMI eARC and optical audio for inputs, and it can connect to devices via Bluetooth. My interest in this model has been piqued ever since RTINGS named it one of its favorite budget-friendly soundbars.\n[Product: Govee Outdoor Lamp Post | https://www.amazon.com/Govee-Brightness-Integrated-Waterproof-Assistant/dp/B0DXDY4Y26/?tag=theverge02-20, https://govee.sjv.io/c/482924/3014037/12845?u=https%3A%2F%2Fus.govee.com%2Fproducts%2Fgovee-outdoor-lamp-post-lights%3Fcurrency%3DUSD%26variant%3D44850372542649%26stkn%3De32faa3ec03e%26utm_source%3Dgoogle%26utm_medium%3Dcpc%26utm_campaign%3DPmax_US_OutdoorLights_220721%26ot_source%3Dgoogle%26ot_medium%3Dpaidads%26ot_cam%3D17814189508%26ot_grp%3D%26ot_ad%3D%26gad_source%3D1%26gad_campaignid%3D17814192391%26gbraid%3D0AAAAABQ7EBRz7SHi1_QGFkOvAnuTFsUdY%26gclid%3DCj0KCQjw_rPGBhCbARIsABjq9cdwMEFGmCpuNYm7iKQFnTk6Dolt5v1-j1HtZxTizQlTRr4mm0CRQRIaAqliEALw_wcB]\n* The 8-piece and 14-piece Ring Alarm Pro home security systems have gotten big discounts ahead of Prime Day. The smaller kit of the two is $209.99 ($90 off) and includes a base station (it doubles as a eero 6 Wi-Fi router), a keypad, four contact sensors for doors or windows, a motion detector, and a range extender for the alarm. The 14-piece set doubles the keypads, contact sensors, and motion detectors. Both include a 30-day trial to Ring Protect plan, which will cost $19.99 per month after the trial.\n[Product: Ring Battery Doorbell Plus (second-gen) | https://www.amazon.com/Ring-Battery-Doorbell-newest-Nickel/dp/B0GGLS1C4W?ref=amzdv_tplus_dp_dsk_bdldp_B0F14N7HHH_B0GGLS1C4W&tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fring-battery-doorbell-plus-newest-model-retinal-2k-with-wide-angle-video-up-to-6x-zoom-night-vision-and-battery-pack-nickel-silver%2FJ39TLSRS6P%2Fsku%2F6672122, https://ring.pxf.io/c/482924/3022805/30431?u=https%3A%2F%2Fring.com%2Fproducts%2Fbattery-doorbell-plus-2nd-gen%2Fcolor%2Fpolishednightnavy]\n[Product: Amazon Fire TV Stick 4K Select | https://www.amazon.com/amazon-fire-tv-stick-4K-select/dp/B0C6W3D4RM?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Famazon-fire-tv-stick-4k-select-newest-model-streaming-device-streaming-in-4k-ai-powered-search-8gb-free-live-tv-black%2FJ39HW66YJK%2Fsku%2F6644637%3Futm_source%3Dfeed%26extStoreId%3D1510%26ref%3D212%26loc%3D18075457655%26gclsrc%3Daw.ds%26gad_source%3D4%26gad_campaignid%3D18075458606%26gbraid%3D0AAAAAD-ORIhSHlGddVnEnW-FqCuPzbvlO%26gclid%3DCjwKCAiAnoXNBhAZEiwAnItcG1TbZE0MTq67hM72gyLFTn2VMnbAmssKQxlB13LpRrmNnprahLMKVBoCL8oQAvD_BwE, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Famazon-fire-tv-stick-4k-select-with-ai-powered-search-and-free-live-tv-2025%2F-%2FA-91651395%23lnk%3Dsametab]\n* Apple’s AirPods Pro 3 have been available at their lowest price to date for the past week or so. Originally $249, the noise-canceling, wireless earbuds are $179 at Amazon and Best Buy — no membership required. Walmart has a product page that lists $169 as a sale price, though it’s out of stock at the time of publication. The AirPods Pro 3 are the latest earbuds from Apple, packing better bass and active noise cancellation than their predecessor, plus the ability to do some light fitness tracking, among other niceties. Read our review.\n[Product: Bose QuietComfort Ultra headphones (second-gen) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FDKQ2FG6?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fbose-quietcomfort-ultra-headphones-2nd-gen-black%2FJ7C5V6W7LP%2Fsku%2F6642778%3Futm_source%3Dfeed%26extStoreId%3D%26ref%3D212%26loc%3DBoseHD%26gclsrc%3Daw.ds%26gad_source%3D1%26gad_campaignid%3D19716535611%26gbraid%3D0AAAAAD-ORIgCZw_CnJk10M8F1qjLLR4Dc%26gclid%3DCj0KCQjw3K7RBhDJARIsAKRtP5SJyrABDYGXfJNISAcq26aFRMFPQHMnwmZKYEisnruApX3XVv_i-YcaAqsKEALw_wcB]\n* Through June 19th (or until supplies last), Woot is offering new customers a small, but welcome $15 discount on the Nintendo Switch 2 console. The $449.99 device drops to $434 with the code NEW15 used at checkout. I know, I know — it’s not much. It may not even cover sales tax associated with the purchase, but a deal’s a deal.\n[Product: Govee Table Lamp Classic | https://www.amazon.com/Govee-Cordless-Classic-Rechargeable-Portable/dp/B0GLM9BBQT/?tag=theverge02-20, https://govee.sjv.io/c/482924/3014037/12845?u=https%3A%2F%2Fus.govee.com%2Fproducts%2Fblack-cordless-led-table-lamp]\n[Product: Apple Watch Series 11 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQFPB851/?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FApple-Watch-Series-11-GPS-42mm-Jet-Black-Aluminum-Case-with-Black-Sport-Band-S-M%2F17828855920, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FQF5BZ8Z/?tag=theverge02-20]\n* Marshall has knocked down prices for some of its home audio products, including its amp-inspired Acton III plug-in speaker. Originally $299.99 (though frequently $200 or so), it’s down to $179.99 in all colorways at Amazon. The Stanmore III that’s bigger and even more powerful, with RCA inputs for plugging in a record player, is $249.99 at Amazon. It’s a much bigger price drop for this one, considering it typically sells for around $300.\n[Product: Gigabyte Gaming OC - Radeon RX 9070 XT graphics card | https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0G2GLV534/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0DS2QG2KW/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20]",
