      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-15-show-hn-veterinarian-turned-founder-ai-lawn-diagnosis",
      "title": "Show HN: Veterinarian turned founder, AI lawn diagnosis",
      "summary": "I know, it's kind of weird. What is a veterinarian doing creating an analysis tool for lawn problems?\nFrankly, the idea was born of my own lawn care struggles. Endless lawn care company fees without any actual improvement. Googling problems and finding generic solutions without regional considerations. One time I overseeded my grass not realizing I had to actually put soil down too.\nOne day, I dec",
      "body": "Want us to send you a copy of your results plus seasonal lawn care tips tailored to your ZIP code and grass type?\nNo spam, ever. Unsubscribe anytime.\nFree · AI-Powered · Localized to Your ZIP\nYour lawn is tryingto tell yousomething.\nUpload photos of your lawn, enter your ZIP code, and get an instant AI diagnosis — with a personalized treatment plan built for your exact region, grass type, and season.\nUpload photos · Enter ZIP · Get your plan instantly\nBetter photos = more accurate diagnosis. Upload up to 4 shots: an overview of the whole lawn, a close-up of the problem, the edge where healthy meets damaged, and a blade or soil detail.\nStand back, capturethe whole yard\nGet within 1–2 ftof the issue\nShow the border wheregood meets bad\nMacro shot of grassblades or soil\n0 of 4 photos · at least 1 required\nOur AI is checking your grass type, regional conditions, and common problems for ZIP\nThree steps to ahealthier lawn.\nNo lawn care expertise required. Our AI does the heavy lifting — you just take a photo.\nTake up to 4 guided photos of your lawn — an overview, a close-up, the healthy/damaged border, and a blade detail. More photos means a more accurate diagnosis.\nYour ZIP determines your climate zone, grass type, and seasonal conditions — making the diagnosis genuinely localized, not generic advice that ignores where you live.\nReceive an instant diagnosis with a tiered treatment plan: DIY products with Amazon links, subscription services, or professional help — you choose what fits your situation.\n\"I had no idea what was killing my lawn every summer. GrassDx diagnosed it as brown patch fungus in seconds and recommended exactly the right treatment. Best lawn I've ever had.\"\n\"The ZIP code feature is genius. It knew I was in the Pacific Northwest and gave me advice specifically for cool-season grass. No generic tips — exactly what I needed.\"\n\"Saved me from calling a lawn service that would've charged $300. The DIY fix worked perfectly and cost $22 from Amazon. I tell every neighbor about this site.\"\nFree · No Account · Instant Results\nReady for a lawnyou're proud of?\nTakes 30 seconds. Upload a photo, enter your ZIP, and get your personalized lawn care plan — completely free.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
