      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-14-dillo-directory-directory-of-useful-sites-that-work-reasonab",
      "title": "Dillo directory – Directory of useful sites that work reasonably well on Dillo",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://dir.dillo-browser.org/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48529645\nPoints: 16\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Directory of useful sites that work reasonably well on Dillo with a focus on\nhuman crafted content. Typically with no JavaScript and modest use of CSS. No\nAlternative frontends to many sites.\nArticles saved from Usenet newsgroups by Norman Yarvin\nBBS text files archive 1980-1995.\nBBS text files archive post 1995.\nLoose collective of rogue archivists, programmers, writers and loudmouths\ndedicated to saving our digital heritage.\n\"Discover articles and blogs on Bear\".\n\"Independent blog posts, ranked by the community. Good stuff bubbles up.\n\"CAPCOM is a public aggregator of subscribable Gemini pages and Gemini\n\"A privacy-first, no-nonsense, super-fast blogging platform\".\n\"Naked blogging platform, for minimalists\".\nOnline library with over 75,000 free eBooks\nHigh quality free public domain eBooks\nSearch a book using the ISBN in multiple sites and databases.\nLibrary for textbooks with an open license.\nForum for art and creative topics (closed on mondays).\n\"A community of like-minded website hobbyists and professionals helping to\nmake the web fruitful and bountiful again\".\n\"Socially motivated website that provides information for protecting your\nSolar-powered magazine covering low technology solutions.\nA magazine for the non-corporate and independent web.\nComputer security and hacker culture magazine since 1985.\nProgramming, security, electronics and similar topics.\nMagazine exploring the small web, indie web, and digital minimalism.\nMarketplace listing with no checkout or shopping cart (UK based).\nText-only version of National Public Radio (US).\nText-only version of Canadian Broadcasting Corporation.\nHand crafted news updated when relevant.\nOpen-access repository of electronic preprints.\nSearch engine for older style and lightweight pages.\nLightweight version of DuckDuckGo search engine.\nArch Linux curated documentation (applicable to many other distros).\nComprehensive list of free software for self-hosting (big!).\nAlternatives to the standard internet stack.\nPOSIX.1-2008 official documentation (see table of contents).\nPractical steps to reduce carbon footprint.\n\"Permacomputing is both a concept and a community of practice oriented\naround issues of resilience and regenerativity in computer and network\nComputing-focused link aggregator with moderated discussion.\nReader-supported news for Linux and free software development.\nLink aggregator with a small social network hosted on a RPi 3.\n\"A collecton of plaintext (and mainly text) websites\".\n\"A guide to navigating the web without JavaScript\".\n\"A list of text-only & minimalist news sites\".\nBMK Lite & Text Only News and other Websites\n\"A List of text only & lightweight, News, Sports, Weather, Search\nEngines, Cooking, Tech News, News Aggregator Websites, and other\n\"Resources page for the Cheapskate's Guide to Computers and the\n\"The Internet is not much without links. We should link more\".\n\"The Bookmarks is a curated list of websites\".\n\"Collection of all bookmarks that I used to save across multiple browsers\n\"A look at search engines with their own indexes\".\nHand-crafted wikis and portfolios for artists and developers.\nBlogs and personal sites from IndieWeb (many images!).",
