      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.versowriter.app\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48519567\nPoints: 24\n# Comments: 12",
      "body": "v1.0.22 on the App StoreBuilt for the Mac.Not ported to it.You open it. You write. That’s the whole thing. $14.99, once.Get Verso on the App Store7-day free trial. No payment until you decide.macOS 14+. $14.99 one-time purchase after trial. No subscription.Writing shouldn’t require a subscription.I switched to Mac and discovered that writing on it is... complicated. Maybe complicated is the wrong word. There is choice, a fair amount of it. But nothing that was working for me.Word wants a subscription. Pages is a lot of app. TextEdit tops out at bold and italic. Others are too single-minded.So I built my own. It does what I need, nothing I don’t, and it never asks me to log in.TomaszBrighton, 2026Built for MacInstant launchRuns offlineZero trackingFocus Mode.Everything else fades.One click. The toolbar goes. The sidebar goes. The paragraph you’re writing stays lit. Everything else gets out of the way.It turns out that’s all you needed. ⌘ShiftFTrack Changes.See every edit.You turn it on. Every insertion gets underlined, every deletion shows through. Accept or reject one at a time, or clear the lot. The sidebar keeps a running list so nothing slips past you.Five page colours.One click to switch.Five backgrounds. One for the essay you’re finishing at midnight. One for the notes you’re taking in bright sun. One for when you just want it to feel like paper.Light or dark. Your call.Verso follows your system appearance, or you can pick one and stick with it. Either way, it looks right.Opens your Word files.No import wizard.Someone sends you a Word file. You open it. Nothing breaks. You send it back. Still nothing breaks.Nobody needs to know you didn’t use Word.VersoWordNo ribbon. No clutter. Your file Same document. Drag to compare.Works with your filesWrite in your language.Verso speaks 16 languages. Every menu, label, and tooltip is translated natively, not machine-translated after the fact.Follows your macOS language setting. No configuration needed.What makes Verso differentCommentsSelect text and add a comment. Resolve when done. The sidebar lists every comment with its resolved state. Round-trips through .docx.Markdown round-tripOpen .md files, edit as rich text with syntax-highlighted code blocks, save back as Markdown. Headings, lists, tables, and formatting all preserved.Syntax highlighting22 languages including Swift, Python, TypeScript, Rust, and Go. Paste code into your document and it highlights automatically. Works in both light and dark mode.Everything elseFull formattingBold, italic, underline, strikethrough, superscript, subscript, text colour, highlightingTablesInsert, resize, cell backgrounds, borders, row and column managementPage layoutA4, Letter, Legal. Portrait or landscape. Custom margins. Multi-columnFootnotes & TOCPopover editing, auto-generated Table of Contents with page numbersHeaders & footersPage numbers, custom text, and layout guidesListsBullets, numbers, letters, Roman numerals. Five bullet stylesFind & ReplaceCase-sensitive, whole-word, regex. Match counterLaTeX mathPaste equations from ChatGPT or Gemini. Inline and display mathCustomizable toolbarDrag to reorder, toggle groups on or off. Your layout persists across sessionsPinch-to-zoomTrackpad pinch gesture to zoom in and out of your documentDocument outlineSidebar showing all headings for quick navigation through long documentsMermaid diagramsFlowcharts, sequence diagrams, and more render live in Markdown documentsStyle redefinitionRight-click any style to update it to match the current selectionExport to PDFPrint-ready PDF export from any documentWatermarksText watermarks for drafts and confidential documents16 languagesFull UI localization: English, Japanese, Spanish, Arabic, Polish, Chinese, French, Korean, and more“If you have bugs, questions, hopes, or dreams, feel even more free to get in touch.”TomaszPay once. Write forever.Most writing apps are either too much app or too much cost. Verso is neither.No subscriptions. No recurring charges. Verso is yours for life.Office 365$99.99per yearBut you can’t just buy Word.Ulysses$49.99per year, foreveriA Writer$49.99one-time (Mac only)Best valueVerso$14.99one-time, yours forever$14.99 one-time. No subscription, ever. All updates included.Click to previewLoved by Mac writersReal reviews from people who switched from Word, Pages, and other writing apps.\"A great lightweight writing app. It's fast, simple, and does exactly what I need without getting in the way.\"Dr-GregExcellent MS Word Replacement\"Didn't expect much, but this is solid! Opens .docx files perfectly and launches instantly. No bloat, no subscription.\"MacUser_2026Simple and effective\"Finally, a Mac word processor that feels like it was built for Mac. Clean, fast, and the focus mode is a game-changer.\"Sarah_WritesBest Mac-native option",
