    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-13-shepherd-s-dog-a-game-by-the-most-dangerous-ai-model",
      "title": "Shepherd's Dog: A Game by the Most Dangerous AI Model",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://koenvangilst.nl/lab/claude-fable-shepherds-dog\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48513728\nPoints: 155\n# Comments: 118",
      "body": "A few days ago, Anthropic released the model that was supposedly too dangerous for the world to see. I wanted to give it a try using my personal benchmark: can it build a game idea I've had for years, in a single shot?\nThe model started with a very long reasoning session, and after 45 minutes and more than €20 worth of tokens (!), it happily reported that \"Shepherd's Dog is complete — a single 2,319 line index.html with zero dependencies.\"\nYou can watch the video below or give the game a try It's really fun and exactly how I imagined it. For me this is the first time an AI model is able to create this for me in one go:\nPlay the game here: vnglst.github.io/when-ai-fails/shepards-dog/claude-fable-5/index.html\nOther attempts with earlier models: github.com/vnglst/when-ai-fails/blob/main/shepards-dog/README.md",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "vnglst",
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-13T05:44:46.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://koenvangilst.nl/og/claude-fable-shepherds-dog.png",
