      "body": "Zoo celebrates birth of second pair of Sengi pups It says Nuru and Mela are proving to be \"exceptional parents\". Beds, Herts & BucksWatch: Peru police dress up as World Cup mascots during drug raidPeruvian police officers disguised themselves as 2026 World Cup mascots to break into the home of a suspected drug dealer - and football fan.Latin AmericaWatch: David Beckham receives star on the Hollywood Walk of FameThe former footballer was joined by his wife Victoria Beckham and their children, as well as actor Tom Cruise.Was it an overreaction to cancel buses and trains after disorder?Translink apologised, saying \"it was prioritising keeping staff, passengers, and the wider public safe\".Northern IrelandSchool 'blown away' by dog birthday video reactionThe clip subsequently went viral, something co-headteacher Paul Bailey says took them by surprise.Family & EducationMoment 500ft Welsh landmark is demolished in controlled explosionThe power station was completed in 1964 and has been a landmark in the Vale of Glamorgan for decades. WalesGovernment crackdown on illegal migrants to 'intensify' The UK government says its going to crackdown on illegal migrants living in Northern Ireland.Northern IrelandBaby elephant plays ball in time for World CupIt is seen playing with a ball in his enclosure, only two days after his arrival.Beds, Herts & BucksChurch bells heard for first time in 100 yearsThe peal of a full set of a 14th Century church's bells is heard once again across a parish.NorfolkOne-minute World NewsWatch the latest news summary from BBC World News. International news updated 24 hours a day.Watch: Three things to know about SpaceX's stock market debutThe BBC's Samira Hussain explains everything you need to know about SpaceX's historic IPO.Thailand’s royal household announces death of Princess BajrakitiyabhaThe princess had been in a coma for more than three years, and was 47 at the time of her death.Asia'I was employee number one': SpaceX co-founder reacts to firm's market debutThe BBC's Michelle Fleury spoke to Tom Mueller, who was one of the company's founders alongside Elon Musk in 2002.Mean Girls run at Belfast's Grand Opera House cancelled due to unrestVivian Panka, who plays Regina George, says she has been scared to leave her room.Northern IrelandNurse chased by masked men as second night of disorder breaks outA nurse was chased into the Ulster Hospital by four masked men as disorder continued for a second night.Northern IrelandBBC Newsline Signed SummaryA signed summary of BBC Newsline.Drone shows huntsman's hounds killing hare on farmA huntsman is seen on aerial footage along with hounds, which chase down a hare in a field.EnglandA sneak peek inside Mexico’s iconic Azteca Stadium before World Cup kickoffThe BBC's Will Grant got access inside the renovated venue ahead of the first game of the tournament.Latin AmericaWatch: What does a Northamptonshire scone taste like?Scone fans get to sample a regional treat created by bakery students for a competition.NorthamptonshireCould this be Britain's fittest farmer?David Wheatley says he trains using old tyres and gas canisters.Cambridgeshire",
