      "id": "hackernews-2026-06-11-nextcloud-hub-26-spring-built-together-designed-for-the-futu",
      "title": "Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring: Built together, designed for the future",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://nextcloud.com/blog/nextcloud-hub26-spring/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48490715\nPoints: 101\n# Comments: 72",
      "body": "A decade of privacy, sovereignty and collaboration\nTen years ago, we built Nextcloud to solve a problem that is even more pressing today: the dependence on centralized, proprietary software that threatens our privacy and sovereignty. Organizations need a future-proof framework to replace centralized, legacy collaboration tools. One that only open source can provide.\nFrom home clouds to large-scale enterprises, governments and industries, people are increasingly adopting Nextcloud as their digital workspace. It gives you choice: who controls your data, what tools you use and what it costs, how much privacy for you is enough privacy.\nTrue to the open source way, Nextcloud is a platform running on joint stewardship: our contributing community, our partners and our customers, and Nextcloud as company – a guarantor of stability and direction. We share what we build, so it’s built the best possible way. Innovation minus the Big Tech economics.\nToday we present Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring, our anniversary release. It gives you even more choice for your tools, a refined UI, stress-free collaboration, and the new platform strategy that enables developers to benefit even more from our vast ecosystem.\nSince 2016, Nextcloud GmbH has steered the direction, while Nextcloud and its platform remain a dedicated work of thousands. Developers, testers, translators, writers, and designers, some shaping Nextcloud from its inception, some joined us along the way.\nCustomers and partners, service providers, universities and research organizations, and a variety of public entities contributing to Nextcloud and giving it valuable guidance. Nextcloud is here because we all care.\nThanks to the best community in the world 💙\nNextcloud is not owned by anyone,it is owned by everyone. There’s no single entity that is more powerful than our community.\nWe want to thank everyone who has been part of this movement over the past 10 years. Every contributor to Nextcloud and to this latest release. Together, you have shaped Nextcloud and advanced the entire open source movement.\nKudos to everyone who contributed to Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring! 💪\nCollabora Productivity based on work of Frank Karlitschek, Victor Dubiniuk\nJonne Haß, Arno Welzel, Florian Forestier\nRoeland Jago Douma (original author)\nNextcloud Two-Factor Authentication Working Group\nA decade of privacy, sovereignty and collaborationBuilt together 🤝Thanks to the best community in the world 💙Great design, further refinedYour choice: Nextcloud Office powered by Collabora or Euro-OfficeNextcloud Office by Euro-OfficeNextcloud Office by Collabora OnlineCustomization, AI chat, and interoperability: Updates in Collabora Online ✨AI chat sidebar 💬Customizable status bar ⚙️Presentations: Slide sections and dynamic zoom 🏞️Spreadsheets: smoother calculations and data organization 🔢Euro-Office, a sovereign open source office built in Europe 🇪🇺True open source, shared governance 🌱Spotty connection? Nextcloud Text has your back 📶Easier data organization and sharing in Nextcloud Tables ♟️Improved search and Smart Picker in Nextcloud CollectivesStress-free teamworkCall from anywhere and organize conversations 💬More in Nextcloud Talk: private replies to group messages, Voice Rooms, desktop client improvementsNextcloud Groupware: delegate more, collaborate better 🤾Better interoperability in Nextcloud Mail 📮Nextcloud Deck: Gantt charts, card dependencies, and more 📊New agent tools and improved performance in Nextcloud Assistant 🧠Universal Search and more app data 🔎Chat and context menu action on mobile 🤳Improved performance and backend interoperability ⚡️Flexible UI 📍Where apps become a team: Nextcloud platform for developersEmpowering independent developers 💙Anna LarchAnnouncing Nextcloud ISV program 🌱API updates 👩‍💻New integrations 🧩Featured new community apps 🎁MastermindLinkboardCountdownWeek PlannerPantryThe upkeep is on us 🧹Compliance for enterprises with Nextcloud GovernanceJoin the Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring webinarDesigned for the future 💪Try the new features onlineGet your own Nextcloud HubDiscover Nextcloud Enterprise*Explore all Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring features\nIn Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring, we elevate the interface with a refined, lighter design and multiple subtle improvements. Consider it a birthday glow-up!\nYour apps are now available via focused waffle menu for centralized access to all your apps. It reduces distraction and uses the interface space efficiently as your your library grows.\nWe adjusted the shades in the left-side app navigation to reduce distraction and avoid visually competing with the primary button.\nActive tab in the right sidebar is now tinted and features a smaller, animated highlight bar.\nBased on the feedback from our community, we also improved usability and design in the settings and across many apps in Nextcloud Hub, including multiple minor papercut issues.\nYour choice: Nextcloud Office powered by Collabora or Euro-Office\nWe have always offered multiple office suite options, letting you choose the integration that best fits your interoperability needs, user experience or security preferences. Today we are introducing a new office app and a range of improvements around Nextcloud Office.\nToday we are introducing Euro-Office. It is available as second default office suite option in Nextcloud Office, alongside Collabora-based suite of apps.\nIf you run a Nextcloud AIO, you can easily switch between two office options in the Nextcloud AIO web interface.\nLets find out what’s new in the office apps in Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring.\nCustomization, AI chat, and interoperability: Updates in Collabora Online ✨\nThe Collabora-based suite in Nextcloud Office gets updates across all editors with Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring, improving interoperability and delivering smoother experience.\nThe new sidebar lets users chat with Nextcloud Assistant alongside the document. Like all AI tools in Nextcloud, it is optional and fully configurable.\nChoose which indicators you want to see in your status bar, like word count, zoom controls, language selector, page numbers. Your preferences are remembered between sessions.\nPresentations: Slide sections and dynamic zoom 🏞️\nThe presentation editor now supports slide sections, making it much easier to structure and navigate larger presentations by grouping the slides.\nWhen you resize your window, presentation zoom is now re-calculated automatically to give you the optimal fit in both dimensions.\nSpreadsheets: smoother calculations and data organization 🔢\nNeed to quickly randomize data for sampling, demos, testing, or even selecting a winner? Spreadsheet editor now includes a new Shuffle action in the Sort split button.\nCleaning sheets is safer now: deleting a cell that breaks formulas elsewhere triggers a warning so you can confirm or undo before the broken #REF! references affect calculations.\nYou can now resize the autofilter dropdown in spreadsheets. Drag its edge to make it taller or wider so you can see more entries at once without scrolling. It’s particularly helpful for filters with long item lists.\nThere are many other improvements in the Collabora Online-based Nextcloud Office app. Find the full list of key updates in the section below this blog.\nEuro-Office, a sovereign open source office built in Europe 🇪🇺\nEuro-Office is here. It is a complete office suite with a set of collaborative editors for text documents, spreadsheets, presentations and PDF files.\nIt features seamless collaboration, maximum compatibility with Microsoft Office files, and, thanks to its distinct architectural approach, delivers excellent browser performance while reducing server load. Features like Undo/Redo and Track Changes mode work independently in collaboration, making it flawless for multi-user editing sessions.\nEuro-Office lets you edit Nextcloud documents not only in the browser, but also on the go, directly within the Nextcloud app available on iOS and Android.\nFor example, we already integrated the Smart Picker so you can insert links to content all across Nextcloud like Deck cards, calendars, chat rooms, files, locations and more. We also integrated the Nextcloud Assistant and Euro Office works with the Nextcloud file conversion API. That allows it to convert documents into other types, like a spreadsheet in a CSV or a markdown file into a PDF.\nTrue open source, shared governance 🌱\nEuro-Office is a coordinated European initiative bringing together open source organizations, independent developers and civil society actors under a shared governance framework. Read more about the project and the next steps for Euro-Office in our latest announcement.\nSpotty connection? Nextcloud Text has your back 📶\nWe are constantly improving our markdown editor to make it more robust when your connection is unstable. Now it simply works even if you go fully offline, for up to 5 minutes.\nIn Nextcloud Collectives, our knowledge sharing app based on Nextcloud Text, you can now browse pages from your cache even while offline, if you have opened them before.\nEasier data organization and sharing in Nextcloud Tables ♟️\nOrganizing data in your tables now takes less effort. You can now reorder, sort and pin table columns in a few clicks. Easily reorder views in your Tables-based applications. And additionally, you can delete and duplicate rows.\nGet more done together: share tables via public links with an ability to edit table contents.\nAnd finally, you can turn on notifications to get alerted about new actions with table or view data.\nImproved search and Smart Picker in Nextcloud Collectives\nFinding and sharing pages is now easier. We made search results better and more relevant by using a new database search in Nextcloud Collectives. When using Smart Picker to share a page, you will see page suggestions based on recently changed pages.\nLet’s find a better balance in fast-paced teamwork. For those of you in motion between chats, emails, events, and projects, Nextcloud delivers one connected experience. With Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring, we make it even more integrated, adaptable, and simple.\nCall from anywhere and organize conversations 💬\nWhen a task calls for quick question, start a call instantly from anywhere. Just click on the avatar of the person you need to reach, start the call, and chat while keeping on with your work.\nAre you a chat person? We also made organizing all your conversations a lot easier. First, you can sort conversations alphabetically or by recent activity to find relevant chats easier.\nNow your project chats, team conversations and off-topic rooms are nicely grouped. Assign tags to your conversations and group them by these tags.\nMore in Nextcloud Talk: private replies to group messages, Voice Rooms, desktop client improvements\nBy popular demand, we added a few more features in Nextcloud Talk. For example, you can reply to a group chat message privately to keep the conversation focused, and the reply will include the quote of the original message.\nWe also added Voice Rooms with ongoing calls, allowing you to join a call instantly, and improved noise suppression with a more advanced option.\nIn our desktop client, we added support for connecting multiple accounts, so you can add your work, personal or other Nextcloud Hub instances. We also enabled automatic updating of the client.\nNextcloud Groupware: delegate more, collaborate better 🤾\nIn a big team, the more dependencies, the more you need to delegate. Managing a shared inbox, covering for a colleague on leave, or handling customer communication on someone’s behalf, delegation in Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring keep things moving:\nNextcloud Mail: you can read and reply to emails on behalf of another person.\nNextcloud Calendar: you can create events on behalf of another person and accept event invitations.\nNow you can also forward calendar invites to others and they can accept them, adding an event to their own calendar. Event organizers can disable invite forwarding to protect sensitive meetings.\nBetter interoperability in Nextcloud Mail 📮\nWe enabled full read-write support for external CalCAV and CardDAV, adding an ability to connect external calendars and address books to yours respectively. For example, you can browse events from Zimbra, OpenXchange, or a private calendar server, and all the events you create in Nextcloud will appear there.\nNextcloud Deck: Gantt charts, card dependencies, and more 📊\nMore for your project management in Nextcloud Deck. We introduce card dependencies and start dates in addition to end dates, so you can get a better overview of your tasks’ timeline.\nYou can build Gantt charts based on your Nextcloud Deck boards, mapping all the task dependencies and timelines onto one view. Drag’n’drop cards, choose between day/week/month views and color-code your timelines.\nThat’s not all updates for your next project. Assign whole teams and groups to cards and see card authors. Choose a board to open by default when launching Nextcloud Deck. Customize your boards: define column for completed tasks and add custom card backgrounds.\nNew agent tools and improved performance in Nextcloud Assistant 🧠\nNextcloud Assistant helps you be confident about what happens to your data tomorrow. It gives you what data-hungry cloud chats can’t: control and choice. Know how your AI works, choose where it runs, and pick only the tools you need.\nWith Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring, we give it more hands and make it even more powerful.\nUniversal Search and more app data 🔎\nNextcloud Assistant can now use Unified Search in your Nextcloud Hub to find any items based in fewer steps. This works via Context Agent feature.\nIt also knows data in your apps better, helping you find items and perform new actions in file system, emails, tasks, forms, Nextcloud Deck boards and cards, and more.\nChat and context menu action on mobile 🤳\nYou can now chat with Nextcloud Assistant on mobile. And it’s better integrated with your device: use the context menu on iOS or Android to ask the Assistant to work with any text you come across.\nImproved performance and backend interoperability ⚡️\nNextcloud Assistant receives better background job scheduling and configurability, delivering faster replies from context-enabled tasks and many other performance improvements. We also worked on the architecture, enabling support for Kubernetes for Context Chat features and LLM2.\nYou can now drag and resize the Nextcloud Assistant UI. This let’s you work in any other apps while using Nextcloud Assistant on the side.\nWhere apps become a team: Nextcloud platform for developers\nNextcloud Hub highly adaptable across industries and use cases. It’s designed to be extended, integrated and adapted, rather than limiting the choices of the administrator to a single vendor or a controlled selection of integrations. We empower independent developers and vendors even more through Nextcloud platform.\nNextcloud is built together, and we want to make it easier to participate. We are revising our developer support strategy, which includes cleaning up our documentation, improving tutorials, introducing more stable APIs and establishing better communication channels with developers.\nTo put this into practice, we are launching a dedicated Developer Relations team led by Anna Larch. Say hi!\nNextcloud is a mature, widely adopted ecosystem, and therefore works perfectly as a development platform. We want to empower developers to build reliable apps and tools, using the collective knowledge of our own developers and the community. This, in turn, will provide organizations the building blocks for digital workspaces that suits their unique needs.Anna LarchDeveloper Relations\nAnnouncing Nextcloud ISV program 🌱\nNextcloud is more than a company or a product. It’s a platform, one we shape together with our community and organizations in our ecosystem. In the next chapter, we want to be good stewards and do more than just offer our app building tools. We are introducing the Nextcloud ISV program to help independent software vendors (ISVs) grow their audience, promote apps and provide support to their customers via the Nextcloud platform.\nHow the Nextcloud ISV program empowers vendors:\nWe promote your apps in our App Store, offer subscriptions, and facilitate support and documentation.\nYou provide stable, scalable apps with long-term support that answer our standards in privacy, security and run locally.\nRead more and become an Independent Software Partner of Nextcloud. Let’s collaborate!\nKey API updates in Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring include:\nSeveral removed back-end and front-end APIs and libraries\nRead more details about critical API changes in our documentation.\nSecure and compliant video conferencing platform with great interoperability.\nSend files to an Element/Matrix conversation directly from Nextcloud Files.\nWe have also worked on accessibility features of Nextcloud App Store, improving the experience with navigating the pages.\nFeatured new community apps 🎁\nNextcloud version of the popular game Mastermind. Crack a code consisting of five colors within a fixed number of turns.\nCustomizable service dashboard to organize your services in categories, monitor status, and access everything from Nextcloud.\nYour most anticipated releases, in one place! Manage countdowns for games, movies, series, and personal events.\nA simple weekly planner inspired by Tweek, living right inside your Nextcloud. Easy planning with full control over your data.\nHousehold management app to keep your house organized collaboratively with checklists, photo boards, notes and more.\nThe upkeep is on us 🧹\nIt’s a lot of features, but it’s only 4% of what we’ve done. To live up to the trust millions of people are putting in Nextcloud, in this release we focused on stability and refinement.\nWe invested in bug fixing, performance work and improving reliability across everyday workflows. 96% of code change done in this release across all repos are maintenance work, including translations, small UI fixes, stability, security and performance.\nCompliance for enterprises with Nextcloud Governance\nLarge organizations that deal with specific regulations like complex archival rules or freedom-of-information guidelines need more advanced data governance tools. For such organizations we are introducing Nextcloud Governance. This functionality provides tighter control over access to sensitive information, data lifecycle management and compliance processes.\nNextcloud Governance provides an overview of the compliance setup in an organization, and offers a series of tools to track and control data:\nSensitivity labels that control access rights\nAbility to enact legal hold on files and create rules that control data lifecycle\nDocumentation and tools to track the compliance tasks that need to be done\nLooking back at these 10 years together, we also want to look ahead to what’s next. Nextcloud is 100% open source, it’s built together and belongs to everyone and you. Nextcloud Hub ensures your data remains yours forever. And no matter what happens, Nextcloud is here to stay.\nStay confident with Nextcloud Hub. Get started today!\nOnce the update is available, Nextcloud AIO users can upgrade to Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring directly from the Nextcloud AIO interface with a button.\n*The Nextcloud Enterprise version of Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring will become available soon, once we successfully run the additional testing and complete certification.\nExplore all Nextcloud Hub 26 Spring features\nIntegration of calls into the avatar menuVoice Rooms Advanced noise suppressionImproved attachment sharingHighlight non-installed featuresSorting and grouping options for conversations in the listImproved “Reply private”Multi-account support for desktop clientAutomatic updates for desktop clientConversation tags to group conversations\nMail account delegationAbility to delete a Mail thread and its follow-upsGeneral HTML support for the Mail composer\nCalendar delegationForwarding of calendar invitationsSet default reminder per calendarExternal CalDAV read-write\nAI chat sidebarPresentations: slide sectionsNew customizable status bar PDF: Richer commenting experience Spreadsheets: “Shuffle” in Sort dropdownSpreadsheets: #REF! warning when deleting cellsView Changes radio-style menuSpreadsheets: User-resizable autofilter dropdownOnline help dialog overhaulAccessibility polishAbility to edit template files like DOTX, XLTX, and POTX.Improved cursor scrolling outside the canvas\nDefault board pinning“Done” column featureAssigning Teams and groupsCard dependencies / subtasksCreator information on cardsGantt chartIndividual card background colorsStart date for cardsUser migration\nEnhanced attachments support in sidebar tabFile templates for Text attachments menuCustom page pickerOffline browsingUsing Nextcloud database for TNTSearch\nAPI structure improvementDeleting and duplicating rowsAsynchronous import of tables Option to pin a columnPublic sharing with (write) permissionsPush notifications Re-ordering of views in Application/ContextReorder and sort table columns\nAccessibility improvementsExcalidraw catch-up with upstreamImprove template managementRecording improvementsWhiteboard on mobile\nMobile (iOS): Chat with AIMobile: Performance: Cache content of tabsMobile (iOS, Android): share text to Nextcloud AssistantMobile: Showing recent filesMobile:Tag supportMobile: OAEP encrypted push notifications Mobile: Whiteboard on MobileDesktop: Nextcloud Governance features in desktop clientDesktop: Unified SharingDesktop: feature parity improvements\nEmail indexing in Context chatContext agent: faster repliesContext agent: new tool to use Unified SearchContext agent: a range of new toolsWorkflow AI agent: checking if a PDF form is completely filledWorkflow AI agent: Travel cost reimbursement processKubernetes support for LLM2 and Context ChatProviding information about the provider to the userResponsive UI that works on a mobile screenPerformance improvements when multiple users are using assistant in parallelEU AI act: required documentation Draggable and resizable UI\nModernized app management in Nextcloud App StoreNextcloud App Store accessibility improvementsUser OIDC: manage User OIDC providers through OCS endpointsPexip integrationMatrix/ Element integrationAPI updates (see documentation for details)\nNew integration with Windmill that supports standalone instancesImproved Approval app\nMarking and sorting improvementsExternal CardDAV read-write\nNextcloud Governance appNextcloud Governance: Legal holdNextcloud Governance: ArchivingNextcloud Governance: Sensitivity labelsUnified SharingAdmin page settings redesignApp navigation redesignLeft-side navigation design improvementsRedesign of tabs in the sidebarSettings dialog design improvementsAI Act improvements for Suspicious Login",
